<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>

<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

<title>Career Opportunity Hub | Career Intelligence System</title>

<style>

:root{
--navy:#101a2b;
--navy2:#17243a;
--blue:#315a82;
--gold:#d6a85f;
--gold2:#f1d59e;
--cream:#fffaf1;
--text:#e8edf3;
--muted:#aeb9c8;
--green:#6fbd8b;
--red:#d77a6e;
--purple:#9b8bd4;
--border:rgba(214,168,95,.28);
--shadow:0 18px 45px rgba(0,0,0,.28);
}

*{
margin:0;
padding:0;
box-sizing:border-box;
font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

html{
scroll-behavior:smooth;
}

body{
background:
radial-gradient(circle at 15% 10%,rgba(49,90,130,.35),transparent 35%),
linear-gradient(135deg,var(--navy),#0b111c);
color:var(--cream);
line-height:1.6;
}

.container{
max-width:1400px;
margin:auto;
padding:35px 25px 80px;
}

/* =========================
HERO
========================= */

.hero{
min-height:600px;
display:flex;
align-items:center;
justify-content:center;
text-align:center;
padding:70px 25px;
position:relative;
overflow:hidden;
border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}

.hero:before,
.hero:after{
content:"";
position:absolute;
border:1px solid rgba(214,168,95,.15);
border-radius:50%;
pointer-events:none;
}

.hero:before{
width:600px;
height:600px;
right:-220px;
top:-250px;
}

.hero:after{
width:450px;
height:450px;
left:-220px;
bottom:-240px;
}

.hero-content{
max-width:1000px;
position:relative;
z-index:2;
}

.eyebrow{
display:inline-block;
padding:8px 17px;
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:30px;
color:var(--gold2);
font-size:.78rem;
font-weight:bold;
letter-spacing:1.5px;
text-transform:uppercase;
margin-bottom:22px;
background:rgba(214,168,95,.08);
}

.hero h1{
font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);
line-height:1.03;
margin-bottom:25px;
}

.hero h1 span{
color:var(--gold);
}

.hero p{
max-width:850px;
margin:auto;
font-size:1.18rem;
color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
ORIENTATION
========================= */

.orientation{
margin-top:-35px;
position:relative;
z-index:5;
background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1c2b42,#142033);
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:20px;
padding:25px;
box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.orientation-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
gap:1px;
background:var(--border);
}

.orientation-item{
background:#17243a;
padding:22px;
text-align:center;
}

.orientation-item strong{
display:block;
font-size:1.5rem;
color:var(--gold);
margin-bottom:5px;
}

.orientation-item span{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:.9rem;
}

/* =========================
SECTIONS
========================= */

.section{
margin-top:75px;
}

.section-heading{
max-width:900px;
margin-bottom:30px;
}

.section-heading h2{
font-size:2.35rem;
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:10px;
}

.section-heading p{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:1.05rem;
}

/* =========================
DECISION CARDS
========================= */

.decision-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));
gap:22px;
}

.decision-card{
background:linear-gradient(145deg,#1b2a40,#121c2d);
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:18px;
padding:30px;
position:relative;
overflow:hidden;
transition:.3s;
}

.decision-card:hover{
transform:translateY(-5px);
border-color:var(--gold);
box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.number{
font-size:.78rem;
font-weight:bold;
color:var(--gold);
letter-spacing:2px;
}

.decision-card h3{
font-size:1.4rem;
margin:12px 0;
}

.decision-card p{
color:var(--muted);
margin-bottom:18px;
}

.solution{
border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
padding-top:16px;
color:var(--green);
font-size:.9rem;
font-weight:bold;
}

/* =========================
PROBLEM MAP
========================= */

.problem-map{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
gap:18px;
}

.problem{
padding:27px;
border-radius:16px;
background:#121d2e;
border-top:4px solid var(--gold);
}

.problem h3{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:10px;
}

.problem p{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:.95rem;
}

.problem small{
display:block;
margin-top:15px;
color:var(--green);
font-weight:bold;
}

/* =========================
INTELLIGENCE MATRIX
========================= */

.matrix{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
gap:15px;
}

.matrix-card{
padding:25px;
background:#151f30;
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
border-radius:16px;
}

.matrix-card h3{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:10px;
}

.matrix-card p{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:.9rem;
}

.matrix-number{
font-size:2.2rem;
font-weight:bold;
color:var(--gold);
margin-bottom:8px;
}

/* =========================
CAREER ECONOMICS
========================= */

.economics{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;
gap:25px;
}

.economics-main,
.economics-side{
background:#17243a;
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:22px;
padding:32px;
}

.economics h2{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:15px;
}

.economics p{
color:var(--muted);
}

.factor{
margin-top:22px;
}

.factor-header{
display:flex;
justify-content:space-between;
margin-bottom:7px;
}

.factor-header strong{
color:var(--cream);
}

.factor-header span{
color:var(--gold);
font-weight:bold;
}

.bar{
height:12px;
background:#0e1624;
border-radius:20px;
overflow:hidden;
}

.bar span{
display:block;
height:100%;
background:var(--gold);
}

.equation{
margin-top:25px;
padding:20px;
background:#101a2b;
border-radius:14px;
color:var(--gold2);
font-size:1.05rem;
font-weight:bold;
text-align:center;
}

/* =========================
OPPORTUNITY PORTFOLIO
========================= */

.portfolio{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);
gap:14px;
}

.portfolio-card{
background:#121d2e;
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
border-radius:15px;
padding:23px 16px;
text-align:center;
}

.portfolio-card strong{
display:block;
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:9px;
}

.portfolio-card span{
font-size:.85rem;
color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
CASE STUDY
========================= */

.case-study{
background:
linear-gradient(
135deg,
rgba(49,90,130,.35),
rgba(214,168,95,.08)
);
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:24px;
padding:38px;
}

.case-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
gap:20px;
margin-top:25px;
}

.case-column{
background:rgba(8,15,26,.65);
border-radius:16px;
padding:25px;
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
}

.case-column h3{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:12px;
}

.case-column p{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:.94rem;
}

/* =========================
DECISION ENGINE
========================= */

.engine{
background:#151f30;
border:1px solid var(--border);
border-radius:24px;
padding:35px;
}

.engine-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
gap:22px;
margin-top:25px;
}

.engine-card{
background:#101a2b;
padding:25px;
border-radius:16px;
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
}

.engine-card h3{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:12px;
}

.engine-card p{
color:var(--muted);
}

.engine-card strong{
display:block;
margin-top:15px;
color:var(--green);
}

/* =========================
RESEARCH / FACTS
========================= */

.research{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
gap:20px;
}

.research-card{
background:#17243a;
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
padding:28px;
border-radius:18px;
}

.research-card .source{
font-size:.75rem;
color:var(--gold);
text-transform:uppercase;
letter-spacing:1px;
margin-bottom:10px;
}

.research-card h3{
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:10px;
}

.research-card p{
color:var(--muted);
font-size:.92rem;
}

/* =========================
FINAL SYSTEM
========================= */

.final-system{
margin-top:75px;
padding:50px 35px;
border-radius:25px;
background:
linear-gradient(
135deg,
#243b55,
#17243a
);
border:1px solid var(--border);
box-shadow:var(--shadow);
}

.final-system h2{
font-size:2.4rem;
color:var(--gold2);
margin-bottom:15px;
}

.final-system > p{
max-width:850px;
color:var(--muted);
margin-bottom:30px;
}

.system-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);
gap:15px;
}

.system-step{
padding:22px;
background:rgba(8,15,26,.5);
border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
border-radius:14px;
}

.system-step strong{
display:block;
font-size:1.15rem;
color:var(--gold);
margin-bottom:8px;
}

.system-step span{
font-size:.87rem;
color:var(--muted);
}

/* =========================
FOOTER
========================= */

footer{
margin-top:70px;
padding:40px 25px;
text-align:center;
border-top:1px solid var(--border);
color:var(--muted);
}

footer strong{
color:var(--gold2);
}

/* =========================
RESPONSIVE
========================= */

@media(max-width:1000px){

.orientation-grid{
grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);
}

.problem-map{
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

.matrix{
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

.economics{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.portfolio{
grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);
}

.case-grid{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.research{
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

.system-grid{
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

}

@media(max-width:650px){

.container{
padding-left:18px;
padding-right:18px;
}

.hero{
min-height:520px;
}

.hero h1{
font-size:2.6rem;
}

.hero p{
font-size:1rem;
}

.orientation-grid,
.problem-map,
.matrix,
.research,
.system-grid{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.portfolio{
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
}

.section{
margin-top:55px;
}

}

</style>

</head>

<body>


<!-- =========================
HERO
========================= -->

<section class="hero">

<div class="hero-content">

<div class="eyebrow">
Career Opportunity Intelligence
</div>

<h1>
Stop Searching Randomly.
<br>
<span>Start Thinking Strategically.</span>
</h1>

<p>
A career opportunity is not simply a job opening. It is a temporary alignment
between your capabilities, evidence, positioning, timing, market demand,
relationships, and the problems an organization needs solved.
</p>

</div>

</section>


<div class="container">


<!-- =========================
ORIENTATION
========================= -->

<section class="orientation">

<div class="orientation-grid">

<div class="orientation-item">
<strong>01</strong>
<span>Diagnose the Constraint</span>
</div>

<div class="orientation-item">
<strong>02</strong>
<span>Increase Capability</span>
</div>

<div class="orientation-item">
<strong>03</strong>
<span>Create Evidence</span>
</div>

<div class="orientation-item">
<strong>04</strong>
<span>Increase Opportunity Surface</span>
</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
STARTING POINT
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Your Career Problem Determines Your Strategy
</h2>

<p>
Two people can submit 100 applications and experience completely different
results because their bottlenecks are different. Diagnose before acting.
</p>

</div>


<div class="decision-grid">


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
01 / DIRECTION
</div>

<h3>
You Have Too Many Possible Futures
</h3>

<p>
The problem is not a lack of options. It is an inability to compare options
using meaningful criteria.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: opportunity cost + skill transfer + market demand + learning cost
</div>

</div>


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
02 / CAPABILITY
</div>

<h3>
The Target Requires Skills You Do Not Have
</h3>

<p>
Applying harder will not solve a capability gap. The missing capability must
first be identified and developed.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: skill decomposition → deliberate practice → project application
</div>

</div>


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
03 / EVIDENCE
</div>

<h3>
You Know More Than Your Resume Shows
</h3>

<p>
Knowledge has limited signaling power when another person cannot evaluate
what you can actually produce.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: projects + outcomes + demonstrations + documented decisions
</div>

</div>


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
04 / TRANSLATION
</div>

<h3>
Your Experience Does Not Match the Job Title
</h3>

<p>
Your previous work may contain transferable capabilities hidden behind
different terminology.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: task → capability → business outcome → target-role language
</div>

</div>


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
05 / ACCESS
</div>

<h3>
You Are Qualified but Invisible
</h3>

<p>
A strong candidate can still miss opportunities when their search depends on
only one channel.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: applications + referrals + communities + direct outreach + projects
</div>

</div>


<div class="decision-card">

<div class="number">
06 / ECONOMICS
</div>

<h3>
The Career Cannot Support the Life You Want
</h3>

<p>
A career should be evaluated against compensation, stability, mobility,
learning potential, and long-term optionality.
</p>

<div class="solution">
Use: total compensation + trajectory + risk + optionality
</div>

</div>


</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
CONSTRAINT MAP
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
The Career Constraint Map
</h2>

<p>
The most useful question is often not "What should I do?" but "What is
currently preventing progress?"
</p>

</div>


<div class="problem-map">


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Information Constraint
</h3>

<p>
You do not know enough about the occupation, employers, requirements,
compensation, or pathways.
</p>

<small>
Solution → improve information quality before making expensive decisions.
</small>

</div>


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Capability Constraint
</h3>

<p>
You understand the field but cannot yet perform the critical tasks
independently.
</p>

<small>
Solution → practice the actual work, not merely consume information.
</small>

</div>


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Signal Constraint
</h3>

<p>
Your ability exists but employers have little evidence with which to judge
it.
</p>

<small>
Solution → convert capability into observable proof.
</small>

</div>


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Access Constraint
</h3>

<p>
You rarely encounter decision-makers, opportunities, communities, or people
working in the target field.
</p>

<small>
Solution → increase the number of legitimate opportunity surfaces.
</small>

</div>


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Resource Constraint
</h3>

<p>
Time, money, transportation, equipment, or other resources restrict what
you can realistically pursue.
</p>

<small>
Solution → design a pathway around constraints instead of pretending they
do not exist.
</small>

</div>


<div class="problem">

<h3>
Feedback Constraint
</h3>

<p>
You repeatedly perform actions without learning why they succeed or fail.
</p>

<small>
Solution → track outcomes and change one variable at a time.
</small>

</div>


</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
CAREER INTELLIGENCE MATRIX
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
The Six Variables Behind Career Leverage
</h2>

<p>
A useful career strategy treats progress as a system rather than a collection
of disconnected tasks.
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix">


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
01
</div>

<h3>
Capability
</h3>

<p>
What can you actually perform without constant assistance?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
02
</div>

<h3>
Evidence
</h3>

<p>
What observable artifacts demonstrate that capability?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
03
</div>

<h3>
Demand
</h3>

<p>
Do organizations actually need the capability you are developing?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
04
</div>

<h3>
Access
</h3>

<p>
How many legitimate pathways allow your capability to meet demand?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
05
</div>

<h3>
Positioning
</h3>

<p>
Can another person quickly understand why your background is relevant?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
06
</div>

<h3>
Trajectory
</h3>

<p>
Does today's move increase tomorrow's options?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
07
</div>

<h3>
Transferability
</h3>

<p>
Can the capability travel across employers, industries, or job titles?
</p>

</div>


<div class="matrix-card">

<div class="matrix-number">
08
</div>

<h3>
Scarcity
</h3>

<p>
How difficult is the capability to replace relative to the value it creates?
</p>

</div>


</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
CAREER ECONOMICS
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="economics">


<div class="economics-main">

<h2>
Do Not Optimize for Salary Alone
</h2>

<p>
A career decision can look attractive on salary while being weak on
trajectory, learning, stability, or optionality. Think in terms of the
entire economic system around the role.
</p>


<div class="factor">

<div class="factor-header">
<strong>Compensation</strong>
<span>Immediate Value</span>
</div>

<div class="bar">
<span style="width:82%"></span>
</div>

</div>


<div class="factor">

<div class="factor-header">
<strong>Skill Growth</strong>
<span>Future Value</span>
</div>

<div class="bar">
<span style="width:91%"></span>
</div>

</div>


<div class="factor">

<div class="factor-header">
<strong>Transferability</strong>
<span>Optionality</span>
</div>

<div class="bar">
<span style="width:86%"></span>
</div>

</div>


<div class="factor">

<div class="factor-header">
<strong>Market Demand</strong>
<span>Opportunity</span>
</div>

<div class="bar">
<span style="width:88%"></span>
</div>

</div>


<div class="factor">

<div class="factor-header">
<strong>Stability</strong>
<span>Risk Control</span>
</div>

<div class="bar">
<span style="width:73%"></span>
</div>

</div>


</div>


<div class="economics-side">

<h2>
Career Option Value
</h2>

<p>
One of the most powerful questions is whether a position creates better
options after you leave it.
</p>


<div class="equation">

Career Value =
<br><br>

Current Reward
+
Skill Growth
+
Network Growth
+
Future Options
−
Opportunity Cost

</div>


<p style="margin-top:20px;">

A lower-paying role can occasionally be strategically superior if it creates
rare skills, credible evidence, valuable relationships, or access to a
rapidly expanding field.

</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
OPPORTUNITY PORTFOLIO
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Stop Having Only One Opportunity Pipeline
</h2>

<p>
Career resilience increases when your future does not depend on a single
employer, application system, credential, or source of income.
</p>

</div>


<div class="portfolio">


<div class="portfolio-card">
<strong>Employment</strong>
<span>Traditional jobs and internal advancement</span>
</div>


<div class="portfolio-card">
<strong>Contract Work</strong>
<span>Shorter engagements that create experience</span>
</div>


<div class="portfolio-card">
<strong>Apprenticeship</strong>
<span>Earn while developing occupational capability</span>
</div>


<div class="portfolio-card">
<strong>Portfolio Work</strong>
<span>Projects that demonstrate independent ability</span>
</div>


<div class="portfolio-card">
<strong>Entrepreneurship</strong>
<span>Build solutions around real customer problems</span>
</div>


</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
CASE STUDY
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
Case Study: The Same Person, Two Career Strategies
</h2>

<p>
Consider a worker with strong customer-service experience who wants to move
into technology.
</p>

</div>


<div class="case-study">

<div class="case-grid">


<div class="case-column">

<h3>
Strategy A — Random Applications
</h3>

<p>
The worker changes their resume repeatedly, applies to dozens of unrelated
technology jobs, collects introductory certificates, and waits for an
employer to recognize the potential.
</p>

</div>


<div class="case-column">

<h3>
Strategy B — Capability Bridge
</h3>

<p>
The worker identifies overlapping capabilities: communication, customer
problem solving, documentation, workflow management, CRM use, data
tracking, and process improvement.
</p>

</div>


<div class="case-column">

<h3>
Strategic Difference
</h3>

<p>
Instead of pretending to already be a technology professional, the worker
builds evidence connecting existing experience to a specific technology
function. The career transition becomes a bridge rather than a leap.
</p>

</div>


</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
DECISION ENGINE
========================= -->

<section class="section">

<div class="section-heading">

<h2>
A Better Way to Evaluate an Opportunity
</h2>

<p>
Before accepting an opportunity, examine what it gives you besides a
paycheck.
</p>

</div>


<div class="engine">

<div class="engine-grid">


<div class="engine-card">

<h3>
What Will I Learn?
</h3>

<p>
Identify the skills, systems, tools, processes, and judgment you will gain.
</p>

<strong>
High-value question: Will these skills remain useful outside this employer?
</strong>

</div>


<div class="engine-card">

<h3>
What Will I Be Able to Prove?
</h3>

<p>
Determine whether the work produces measurable accomplishments or visible
artifacts.
</p>

<strong>
High-value question: What will I be able to demonstrate one year from now?
</strong>

</div>


<div class="engine-card">

<h3>
Who Will I Become Connected To?
</h3>

<p>
Consider managers, peers, customers, vendors, professional communities, and
other relationships.
</p>

<strong>
High-value question: Does this environment expand my professional network?
</strong>

</div>


<div class="engine-card">

<h3>
What Does This Unlock?
</h3>

<p>
Look beyond the immediate position to the roles, industries, credentials,
projects, and opportunities it can make accessible.
</p>

<strong>
High-value question: Does this move increase or decrease my future options?
</strong>

</div>


</div>

</div>

