FINAL SYSTEM
========================= -->

<section class="final-system">

<h2>
The Career Intelligence Operating System
</h2>

<p>
Use this sequence whenever you are considering a career change, learning
something new, evaluating a job, or deciding whether an opportunity deserves
your time.
</p>


<div class="system-grid">


<div class="system-step">

<strong>01 — Diagnose</strong>

<span>
Identify the actual constraint. Do not treat every career problem as a job
application problem.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>02 — Decompose</strong>

<span>
Break the desired role into capabilities, tasks, knowledge, tools, and
behavior.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>03 — Prioritize</strong>

<span>
Find the smallest set of capabilities likely to create the largest increase
in opportunity.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>04 — Build</strong>

<span>
Learn through practice and increasingly difficult real-world problems.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>05 — Prove</strong>

<span>
Convert capability into projects, outcomes, demonstrations, documentation,
and measurable evidence.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>06 — Translate</strong>

<span>
Connect previous experience to the language, problems, and outcomes of the
target field.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>07 — Expand</strong>

<span>
Increase the number of legitimate ways your capability can encounter
opportunity.
</span>

</div>


<div class="system-step">

<strong>08 — Iterate</strong>

<span>
Measure results, identify the bottleneck, change the strategy, and repeat.
</span>

</div>


</div>

</section>


